From 32e59b0770b43464f35c6b9f1dc682e4f81a7462 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:35:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: HDMI 3D: no layout for a connector state
 without its connector

amdgpu_dm_update_stream_scaling_settings() asks amdgpu_dm_stereo_layout()
for the layout of the mode through dm_state->base.connector (linux-9925),
and amdgpu_dm_stereo_layout() read connector->stereo_allowed without
looking at the pointer. The KUnit tests of Linux 7.3
(amdgpu_dm_connector_test.c) call the scaling function with a connector
state of their own that has no connector, as nothing in it needed one
before: five of them (dm_test_update_scaling_rmx_full, _aspect_pillarbox,
_aspect_letterbox, _center and _underscan) ended in a NULL pointer
dereference at amdgpu_dm_update_stream_scaling_settings+0x51.

A connector that is not known signals no 3D layout: amdgpu_dm_stereo_layout()
now gives 0 for it, as for a connector that does not allow stereo. In the
driver every connector state carries its connector, so nothing that is sent
changes.

Checked: the KUnit tests of amdgpu_dm of 7.3 (x86_64 in QEMU, the
.kunitconfig of amdgpu_dm/tests without GCOV and debug information, with
WERROR, built with the compiler of the image): 2021 of 2026 before, 2026
of 2026 with this; amdgpu_dm_connector.o with W=1, no warnings.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index 88ea1b7..2e827f1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -992,7 +992,7 @@ u32 amdgpu_dm_stereo_layout(const struct drm_connector *connector,
 {
 	u32 layout = mode->flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_MASK;
 
-	if (!connector->stereo_allowed ||
+	if (!connector || !connector->stereo_allowed ||
 	    (mode->flags & (DRM_MODE_FLAG_INTERLACE | DRM_MODE_FLAG_DBLSCAN)))
 		return 0;
 
